  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Find integers $a$, $b$ and $c$ for which\n$$\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}=\\sqrt{a+b\\sqrt{c}}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=5$, $b=2$, $c=6$.\n\nSquare the positive sum to obtain $5+2\\sqrt{6}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3})^2&=(\\sqrt{2})^2+2\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{3}+(\\sqrt{3})^2\\\\(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3})^2&=2+2\\sqrt{6}+3\\\\(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3})^2&=5+2\\sqrt{6}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}>0$, it is the positive square root of $5+2\\sqrt{6}$. Thus $a=5$, $b=2$ and $c=6$ give the required equality.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
